{"duration_api_ms":120931,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a80a7480-9a9d-4beb-a156-99a4c08a6e67","total_cost_usd":0.18526,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15644,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12268,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7192},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15644,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12268,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15644},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12268,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15644,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18526,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7192,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"After 4 rounds the feasible front (16 points, normalised hypervolume 0.355) is a one-dimensional ridge at D~3.385 m, bluntness 1.2 and cone 70 deg, parameterised only by flight-path angle from -1.5 to -3.568. Flux and bondline T trade smoothly along it: 227k W/m2 with 417.9 K at -1.5 deg, down to 274.5k W/m2 with 391.1 K at -3.567 deg. Three limits pin this corner. max_g (12) caps |gamma| near 3.57. Heatshield mass fraction caps D near 3.385, with margin 1.4e-4. Bluntness and cone angle sit at the edge of the aero surrogate hull (five geometry or hull failures in the 3.3-3.4 m, 1.2, 68-70 deg neighbourhood). The remaining hypervolume gain is therefore in filling gaps along the ridge and shaving the g limit, not in moving to a new region.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-948029610632, C-17412c93bd7a, C-df9f7a25badc, C-8f79870bde82 and C-1c324800060f are spaced 0.3-0.5 deg apart in gamma, so the ridge has gaps at gamma between -1.5 and -2.0, -2.0 and -2.5, and -2.5 and -3.0.\",\"C-78a9a956afab (gamma -3.567, g 11.994, margin 5e-4) and C-1a745bbcb46d (-3.55, g 11.966) give dg/dgamma of about 1.65 g/deg. That puts g=12 at gamma of about -3.5706.\",\"Mass-fraction margin is 0.0207 at D 3.35 (C-ab6fb1629c20) and 1.4e-4 at D 3.385 (C-948029610632), a slope of about 0.59 per metre. Margin does not depend on gamma, so D max is about 3.3852.\",\"C-c9ba8204e0d2, C-a479cd1dc7b5 and C-bd26f4bc6a38 (bluntness 0.9-1.12, D 3.3-3.35) are dominated by the ridge points at gamma -3.5 (flux 280-300k against 273k), so lower bluntness only raises flux.\",\"C-05edbf22eaa2 (bluntness 1.25), C-3d41ce848a30 (1.21, D 3.38) and C-7db223121090 (cone 69, bluntness 1.2) all fail the cd_fore hull check, and C-e0197c1bd7dc (cone 68) and C-5608a135cebc (cone 60) fail geometry. Bluntness above 1.2 and cone below 70 at bluntness 1.2 are not reachable.\",\"Off-ridge designs such as C-ee99f55de428, C-c72c38c9187a and C-50a0a474d0f6 are infeasible or have flux of 0.5-1.8M W/m2, which is far dominated.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, so g<=12 fixes the steep end of the ridge. Shield mass fraction grows about as D^2 and shrinks slightly with bluntness and cone angle, so D is capped near 3.385 at (1.2, 70). A large D and a blunt, wide cone lower the ballistic coefficient, so peak heating occurs higher in the atmosphere and both flux and T fall. The remaining freedom is gamma. Shallower gamma gives lower flux, from lower dynamic pressure at peak heating, but a longer heat pulse and higher bondline T. The front is therefore a smooth convex curve in gamma at fixed geometry. The plan is to densify it (about 10 fill-ins at 0.1-0.2 deg spacing), push the steep end to the g limit (-3.5695 to -3.570), and spend one probe on the hull edge at bluntness 1.203.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Predicted flux and T are linear interpolations along the existing ridge, so they should be good to about 0.5k W/m2 and 0.3 K. The g-limit points (-3.5695 and -3.570) could tip infeasible if g is slightly nonlinear beyond -3.567. The bluntness 1.203 probe may fail the hull check, which would cost one slot. I am relying on prior knowledge of ballistic-entry scaling only for the mechanism; the numbers come from the table.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow end of the ridge just off the gamma=-1.5 bound.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the low-flux end of the front, where T changes fastest with gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -1.6 with the maximum D of 3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the gap between -1.5 and -2.0 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -1.68.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.68},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds spacing on the steep-T part of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Midpoint of the -1.5 to -2.0 gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-17412c93bd7a\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -1.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Completes coverage between -1.75 and -2.0.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-17412c93bd7a\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the -2.0 to -2.25 region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-17412c93bd7a\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":241000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finer sampling between -2.0 and -2.25.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-17412c93bd7a\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.25 with D 3.385. The existing -2.25 point used D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"It should give a slightly lower-T point than C-2850bd21d3cf.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-df9f7a25badc\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":246700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the gap between -2.25 and -2.5.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-df9f7a25badc\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the gap between -2.5 and -3.0.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-df9f7a25badc\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.95,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Midpoint of the widest remaining gap on the ridge.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8f79870bde82\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -2.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Completes the -2.5 to -3.0 coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8f79870bde82\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -3.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the gap between -3.0 and -3.3. g is about 11.25, so it is feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8f79870bde82\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finer spacing in the -3.0 to -3.3 gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1c324800060f\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the gap between -3.3 and -3.45.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-34735e903ad4\",\"rationale\":\"Ridge fill-in at gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extra spacing near the g-limited end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-34735e903ad4\",\"rationale\":\"gamma -3.5 at D 3.385. Existing -3.5 points used D 3.384 or smaller.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.77,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should be a marginal improvement over C-6ffb6b7edb43.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-78a9a956afab\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to the g limit: extrapolated g is about 11.9987.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274580,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the steep end of the front by about 0.003 deg. The margin is tiny, so it tests where g=12 lies.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-78a9a956afab\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D (3.3851) and gamma -3.5695. The mass margin should stay at about +8e-5 and g at about 11.998.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5695},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the corner can be squeezed on both the D and g limits at once.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Hull-edge probe with bluntness just above 1.2 (1.203). Higher bluntness lowers flux and mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.203},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the cd_fore hull edge lies between 1.2 and 1.21. Success would open a small improvement along the whole ridge; failure costs one slot.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":81575,"type":"result","duration_ms":121011,"uuid":"ad631c54-6ce4-4bc4-89c9-c556015b56fd","ttft_stream_ms":1622,"time_to_request_ms":78,"first_content_frame_ms":1622,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
